"""
Connectors of a rotating electrical machine on a shaft: a shaft `flange`, the two
terminals `p` and `n`, and the electrical power it delivers. The shaft machine and the
generator slots of a ship power plant take components that extend this.
"""
partial component ShaftMachinePorts
  flange = Spline()
  "Positive terminal"
  p = Pin()
  "Negative terminal"
  n = Pin()
  "Electrical power delivered at the terminals [W]: positive when the machine generates, negative when it motors"
  electric_power = RealOutput()
end

"""
Ideal DC machine on a shaft: a back-EMF `k · w` behind a series resistance `R`, with its
housing fixed. It is a composition of `ElectricalComponents.Analog.Basic.RotationalEMF`,
`Resistor` and a `PowerSensor`; no equation of its own beyond naming the sensor output.

There is no field or converter control: the terminal current is
`(k · w - v_terminal) / R`, so the machine generates when its EMF is above the bus
voltage and motors when it is below. No iron, friction or windage loss, no inductance,
no saturation, no rating limit.
"""
component DCShaftMachine
  extends ShaftMachinePorts
  "EMF constant [V·s/rad] (equal to the torque constant [N·m/A]), positive"
  parameter k::Real(min = 0)
  "Series (armature) resistance [Ω], positive: the machine is singular at zero"
  parameter R::Real(min = 0)
  emf = ElectricalComponents.Analog.Basic.RotationalEMF(k = k)
  armature = ElectricalComponents.Analog.Basic.Resistor(R = R)
  sensor = ElectricalComponents.Analog.Sensors.PowerSensor()
  housing = RotationalComponents.Components.Fixed()
relations
  connect(flange, emf.rotor)
  connect(emf.housing, housing.spline)
  connect(emf.p, armature.p)
  connect(armature.n, sensor.pc)
  connect(sensor.nc, sensor.pv, p)
  connect(emf.n, sensor.nv, n)
  electric_power = sensor.power
end

"""
Connectors, commands and observation outputs of a ship power plant: what a hull with a
propeller shaft needs from the machinery, and what the machinery reports. A plant is a
component that extends this, holds its engines, gear, electrical machines and loads as
subcomponents, and supplies the rates, powers and states; this partial integrates them,
so every plant has the same counter semantics.

All quantities are SI. Signs:
- `propeller_flange`: positive angle is ahead rotation. `shaft_power` is positive when
  the plant delivers work to the propeller shaft.
- electrical powers are positive into the bus for sources (`genset_electric_power`,
  `pto_electric_power`) and positive into the consumer for `hotel_electric_power`. A
  shaft machine that takes power from the bus to drive the shaft (power take-in) reports
  a negative `pto_electric_power`.

Fuel is reported per consumer, one engine and one fuel each. `*_fuel_consumed_mass` is a
counter from zero at the start: difference it over an interval, never integrate it.
`*_fuel_extrapolated_mass` is the part metered outside the engine's fuel table; an
interval of the fuel counter is inside the table exactly when the extrapolated counter
did not change over it. `*_sfoc_covered` is the instantaneous table-coverage flag; it is
not a calibration statement, and its value at exactly zero load depends on the engine
model, so use the counter for intervals.

Energies and running times are integrals from zero at the start. `shaft_energy` and
`pto_electric_energy` are signed and are not monotone counters when the power changes
sign. Read counters at the accepted solver steps or pass known kink times as `tstops`;
values between steps are the solver's interpolant. An order that steps is a jump of the
fuel rate: give its time as a `tstops` entry.

The outputs describe one main engine and the generating sets as one aggregate. A plant
with several sets, or one that needs start counts or per-set running times for upkeep,
adds outputs of its own next to these.

Conventional subcomponent names inside a plant: `main_engine`, `gearbox`, `pto`
(optional shaft machine), `genset_engine`, `genset_machine`, `hotel_load`.
"""
partial component ShipPowerPlantPorts
  "Propeller shaft; positive angle is ahead rotation"
  propeller_flange = Spline()
  "Ordered propeller-shaft speed [rpm]"
  shaft_speed_order = RealInput()
  "Hotel (ship service) electrical demand at the bus [W]"
  hotel_power_demand = RealInput()

  "Main engine fuel mass rate [kg/s], never negative"
  main_engine_fuel_mass_rate = RealOutput()
  "Main engine cumulative fuel mass [kg], nondecreasing"
  main_engine_fuel_consumed_mass = RealOutput()
  "Part of the main engine fuel metered outside its fuel table [kg]"
  main_engine_fuel_extrapolated_mass = RealOutput()
  "Main engine fuel table coverage, 0 or 1"
  main_engine_sfoc_covered = RealOutput()
  "Generating set fuel mass rate [kg/s], never negative"
  genset_fuel_mass_rate = RealOutput()
  "Generating set cumulative fuel mass [kg], nondecreasing"
  genset_fuel_consumed_mass = RealOutput()
  "Part of the generating set fuel metered outside its fuel table [kg]"
  genset_fuel_extrapolated_mass = RealOutput()
  "Generating set fuel table coverage, 0 or 1"
  genset_sfoc_covered = RealOutput()

  "Mechanical power delivered to the propeller shaft [W]"
  shaft_power = RealOutput()
  "Work delivered to the propeller shaft [J], signed"
  shaft_energy = RealOutput()
  "Electrical power delivered to the hotel load [W]"
  hotel_electric_power = RealOutput()
  "Electrical energy delivered to the hotel load [J]"
  hotel_electric_energy = RealOutput()
  "Electrical power delivered to the bus by the generating set [W]"
  genset_electric_power = RealOutput()
  "Electrical energy delivered to the bus by the generating set [J]"
  genset_electric_energy = RealOutput()
  "Electrical power delivered to the bus by the shaft machine [W]: positive take-off, negative take-in, zero without one"
  pto_electric_power = RealOutput()
  "Electrical energy delivered to the bus by the shaft machine [J], signed"
  pto_electric_energy = RealOutput()

  "Main engine running state, 0 or 1"
  main_engine_on = RealOutput()
  "Main engine running time [s]"
  main_engine_running_time = RealOutput()
  "Generating set running state, 0 or 1"
  genset_on = RealOutput()
  "Generating set running time [s]"
  genset_running_time = RealOutput()

  variable shaft_work::Real
  variable hotel_work::Real
  variable genset_work::Real
  variable pto_work::Real
  variable main_engine_time::Real
  variable genset_time::Real
relations
  initial shaft_work = 0
  initial hotel_work = 0
  initial genset_work = 0
  initial pto_work = 0
  initial main_engine_time = 0
  initial genset_time = 0
  der(shaft_work) = shaft_power
  der(hotel_work) = hotel_electric_power
  der(genset_work) = genset_electric_power
  der(pto_work) = pto_electric_power
  der(main_engine_time) = main_engine_on
  der(genset_time) = genset_on
  shaft_energy = shaft_work
  hotel_electric_energy = hotel_work
  genset_electric_energy = genset_work
  pto_electric_energy = pto_work
  main_engine_running_time = main_engine_time
  genset_running_time = genset_time
end

"""
Geared diesel propulsion with a diesel generating set on a DC bus, built only from this
library's engine presets and from `RotationalComponents` / `ElectricalComponents`
primitives. It leaves the shaft-machine slot open: `DieselMechanicalPlant` closes it with
nothing, `DieselShaftMachinePlant` with a `DCShaftMachine`.

- `main_engine` (`Propulsion.SyntheticDieselEngineA`) drives `engine_inertia` and, through
  the ideal `gearbox` (engine speed / shaft speed = `gear_ratio`), the `propeller_flange`.
  Its speed demand is `shaft_speed_order · gear_ratio`.
- `genset_engine` (`Propulsion.SyntheticDieselEngineB`) is governed at `genset_rpm` and
  drives `genset_machine`, a `DCShaftMachine` whose EMF equals `V_bus` at that speed.
- `hotel_load` is a conductance `hotel_power_demand / V_bus²` between the bus and
  ground, so it draws the demand at the nominal voltage and slightly less when the bus
  voltage sags under load. `hotel_electric_power` is what it actually receives, and it
  depends on the bus voltage: the same demand gives 396.8 kW in `DieselShipTransit` and
  397.4 kW with the shaft machine. Compare two plants on `hotel_electric_energy`, not on
  the demand.

**Synthetic.** The engine presets are invented round numbers, not manufacturer data; the
gear, machines and bus are ideal elements with round parameters chosen so the plant
suits the sample hull. Nothing here is a model of a real installation. Neither engine has
a stopped state, so both `_on` outputs are 1 and the running times equal the elapsed
time. No gear loss, no engine-driven auxiliaries, no bus capacitance, no protection.
"""
partial component DieselPlantBase
  extends ShipPowerPlantPorts
  "Engine speed divided by propeller-shaft speed"
  parameter gear_ratio::Real = 18
  "Main engine rotating inertia [kg·m²]"
  parameter J_engine::Real = 15
  "Initial main engine speed [rpm]"
  parameter engine_rpm0::Real = 1500
  "Generating set speed [rpm]"
  parameter genset_rpm::Real = 1800
  "Generating set rotating inertia [kg·m²]"
  parameter J_genset::Real = 30
  "Nominal bus voltage [V]: the generating set EMF at `genset_rpm`"
  parameter V_bus::Real = 1000
  "Series resistance of the generating set machine [Ω]"
  parameter R_genset::Real = 0.01

  main_engine = DyadShip.Propulsion.SyntheticDieselEngineA()
  engine_inertia = RotationalComponents.Components.Inertia(J = J_engine)
  gearbox = RotationalComponents.Components.IdealGear(ratio = gear_ratio)
  gear_housing = RotationalComponents.Components.Fixed()
  genset_engine = DyadShip.Propulsion.SyntheticDieselEngineB()
  genset_inertia = RotationalComponents.Components.Inertia(J = J_genset)
  genset_machine = DCShaftMachine(k = V_bus / (genset_rpm * π / 30), R = R_genset)
  hotel_load = ElectricalComponents.Analog.Basic.VariableConductor()
  hotel_sensor = ElectricalComponents.Analog.Sensors.PowerSensor()
  hotel_ambient = ThermalComponents.Sources.FixedTemperature(T = 300.15)
  bus_ground = ElectricalComponents.Analog.Basic.Ground()
  "Propeller-shaft speed [rad/s]"
  variable shaft_w::AngularVelocity
relations
  initial engine_inertia.w = engine_rpm0 * π / 30
  initial genset_inertia.w = genset_rpm * π / 30

  # Propulsion line
  connect(main_engine.flange, engine_inertia.spline_a)
  connect(engine_inertia.spline_b, gearbox.spline_a)
  connect(gearbox.spline_b, propeller_flange)
  connect(gearbox.support, gear_housing.spline)
  main_engine.RPM_demand = shaft_speed_order * gear_ratio
  shaft_w = der(propeller_flange.phi)
  shaft_power = -propeller_flange.tau * shaft_w

  # Generating set and bus
  connect(genset_engine.flange, genset_inertia.spline_a)
  connect(genset_inertia.spline_b, genset_machine.flange)
  genset_engine.RPM_demand = genset_rpm
  connect(genset_machine.p, hotel_sensor.pc, hotel_sensor.pv)
  connect(hotel_sensor.nc, hotel_load.p)
  connect(genset_machine.n, hotel_load.n, hotel_sensor.nv, bus_ground.g)
  connect(hotel_load.heat_port, hotel_ambient.port)
  hotel_load.G = hotel_power_demand / V_bus^2

  # Observation outputs
  main_engine_fuel_mass_rate = main_engine.Inst_Fuel
  main_engine_fuel_consumed_mass = main_engine.Fuel
  main_engine_fuel_extrapolated_mass = main_engine.Fuel_extrapolated
  main_engine_sfoc_covered = main_engine.SFOC_valid
  genset_fuel_mass_rate = genset_engine.Inst_Fuel
  genset_fuel_consumed_mass = genset_engine.Fuel
  genset_fuel_extrapolated_mass = genset_engine.Fuel_extrapolated
  genset_sfoc_covered = genset_engine.SFOC_valid
  hotel_electric_power = hotel_sensor.power
  genset_electric_power = genset_machine.electric_power
  main_engine_on = 1
  genset_on = 1
end

"""
`DieselPlantBase` with the shaft-machine slot empty: propulsion is mechanical, the hotel
load is carried by the generating set alone, and `pto_electric_power` is zero.
"""
component DieselMechanicalPlant
  extends DieselPlantBase
relations
  pto_electric_power = 0
end

"""
`DieselPlantBase` with a `DCShaftMachine` in the shaft-machine slot `pto`, on the engine
side of the gearbox and on the same bus as the generating set.

The machine has no control. Its EMF equals `V_bus` at the engine speed `pto_match_rpm`:
above that speed it feeds the bus and relieves the generating set (power take-off), below
it draws from the bus and helps drive the shaft (power take-in). The current is
`(EMF - bus voltage) / R_pto`, so `R_pto` sets how strongly the power follows the engine
speed; a real shaft generator has a converter or field control instead.
"""
component DieselShaftMachinePlant
  extends DieselPlantBase
  "Engine speed at which the shaft machine EMF equals `V_bus` [rpm]"
  parameter pto_match_rpm::Real = 1500
  "Series resistance of the shaft machine [Ω]"
  parameter R_pto::Real = 0.5
  pto = DCShaftMachine(k = V_bus / (pto_match_rpm * π / 30), R = R_pto)
relations
  connect(pto.flange, engine_inertia.spline_b)
  connect(pto.p, genset_machine.p)
  connect(pto.n, bus_ground.g)
  pto_electric_power = pto.electric_power
end
